_tokens":7173,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct or substantiate the claim that `test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` proves scanner-integration predates/parity coverage and non-vacuous execution: either name the specific new assertion the CL will add (scanner-integration ∈ derived closure AND ∈ vote.needs) or move the non-vacuous-execution proof to a test that actually checks vote.needs / execution-not-skipped.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py docstring: 'every step that runs a repo-local gate file either guards that exact file or carries a # predates-gate-ok marker' — the invariant is the -f guard, not scanner vote coverage","The test's only derived-coverage assertion is `assert set(GUARDED_WORKFLOWS) <= derived` (test_guarded_workflow_floor_is_derived_from_ci_lane_uses_closure) — a subset check, not a scanner-integration presence or non-vacuous-execution proof","b973-b298-9b5d-4765 (the prerequisite that shipped this coverage) states 'This ticket therefore does not recreate or re-land the scanner lane' and 'No scanner workflow … is recreated' — its coverage was deliberately scanner-agnostic"],"finding":"The AC claims `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` proves 'predates-gate/parity coverage includes scanner-integration and prevents a vacuous vote where the new job did not execute on its own introducing change', but the named test (read in full) contains no scanner-integration reference and no vote-parity logic — it only verifies `-f` file-existence guards + a canonical skip message for pre-gate trees, and asserts the manual guarded-workflow floor is a subset of a local-`uses:` closure.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f60ef8cfda5036951","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py proves predates-gate/parity coverage includes scanner-integration…'; Anti-90c7 safety design — 'Non-vacuous proof'","norm_id":"ndcc4fcf7690a9b2f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The promoting CL lands, all named tests pass, yet none of them actually assert scanner-integration is voting or that it executed non-skipped on the introducing change — reproducing the exact 90c7 vacuous-vote class the plan says it prevents"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how scanner-integration is treated on the docs-only route (gated full-only vs unconditional) and require BOTH arms of gerrit-verify.yaml's `vote` normalize CONCLUSION expression to be updated accordingly (full-route: `== 'success'`; docs-only: `== 'skipped'`), so a prose-only change is neither stuck nor vacuously verified.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.005,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gerrit-verify.yaml normalize step CONCLUSION expression (lines 477-504) enumerates every full-route job as `needs.<job>.result == 'success'` for the full arm and `== 'skipped'` for the docs-only arm; a newly-voting lane not added to both arms breaks route-completeness","Plan says only 'Add `scanner-integration` to ... vote normalization' without stating whether scanner-integration gates or is skipped on the docs-only route","test.yml scanner-integration currently runs `if: github.event_name != 'schedule'` (unconditional on push/PR), so its gerrit-verify gating condition (full-only vs always) is a real, unresolved design decision","Incident 90c7 red-every-downstream class (Context) is exactly what a mishandled docs-only arm would reproduce"],"finding":"The plan does not specify how scanner-integration interacts with the docs-only route in gerrit-verify.yaml's `vote` normalize step, which asserts exact per-job route completeness (full-route jobs all `== 'success'`, docs-only-route requires them all `== 'skipped'`). Adding scanner-integration to voting needs without threading it into BOTH arms of the CONCLUSION expression can either leave the vote un-guarded or, if scanner runs on docs-only, force a 'failure' on every prose-only change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f84efae1de4115f1c","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope bullet 2 ('vote normalization') and Anti-90c7 safety design; target file .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml lines 470-504","norm_id":"nd60a7b6aa1b8c460","priority":0.595,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A prose-only (docs-only route) Gerrit change: if scanner-integration is gated full-only it is skipped and the docs-only arm must assert `== 'skipped'`; if it runs unconditionally it is `success` and breaks the docs-only arm's all-skipped requirement -> forced 'failure' -> Verified -1 on every docs change","A full-route change: scanner-integration must be asserted `== 'success'` in the full arm or a scanner failure could still pass normalization"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Gate scanner-integration on the full route only (mirroring build-and-test/optionality's `if: ... route == 'full'`), add `needs.scanner-integration.result == 'success'` to the full-route arm and `needs.scanner-integration.result == 'skipped'` to the docs-only arm of the normalize CONCLUSION expression, and add a parity/normalization assertion covering both arms.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the Scope explicit that gerrit-verify.yaml must gain a `scanner-integration` JOB that calls `./.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` with the Gerrit patchset inputs (not only a vote.needs entry), since the only current scanner entrypoint (gerrit-scanner-verify.yml) is workflow_dispatch-only and unreferenced by the Verified lane.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1833,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[".github/workflows/gerrit-scanner-verify.yml: `on: workflow_dispatch:` only; header comment 'it is not in the Verified vote run's job list and cannot affect that workflow's all-jobs conclusion snapshot'","scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py lines 21-24: 'add the reported job(s) to vote.needs … AND make sure the job actually RUNS in that lane — e.g. by calling the shared reusable workflow with the Gerrit patchset inputs'","test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py line 84: `assert 'scanner-integration' not in workflow['jobs']` — scanner-integration is not a job in gerrit-verify.yaml today, so adding it to needs alone would fail parity"],"finding":"The plan asserts scanner-integration currently 'depends on manual dispatch' and must be wired into automatic Gerrit Verified evaluation, but does not name the concrete gap that today the ONLY Gerrit scanner entrypoint (`gerrit-scanner-verify.yml`) triggers exclusively on `workflow_dispatch` and is not referenced by `gerrit-verify.yaml`; the Scope's edit list ('add to voting needs, vote normalization, aggregation') omits adding a scanner-integration JOB into gerrit-verify.yaml that actually RUNS the reusable on the patchset — which the parity script explicitly requires ('the job actually RUNS in that lane').","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb3dab3e0df8f9eae","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — 'Add scanner-integration to .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml voting needs, vote normalization, and required workflow-conclusion aggregation'","norm_id":"n27c5d0dfb9eb4c72","priority":0.5667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author adds scanner-integration only to vote.needs and normalization without adding the reusable-calling job to gerrit-verify.yaml; parity check fails or the vote aggregates a job that never ran on the patchset"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims